{
    "background_story": "Rocco was a majestic wild mustang that roamed the sun-kissed hills of California. His coat was a rich, dark brown, and his mane was flecked with hints of gold. Rocco's home was amidst the rolling hills and vast plains, where the fragrant tarweed bloomed in abundance. He loved to gallop through the fields, feeling the wind in his mane and the tarweed's sweet scent filling his nostrils. As the seasons changed, Rocco grew to appreciate the tarweed's unique ability to thrive in harsh conditions, and he learned to adapt to the ever-changing landscape. The locals would often spot Rocco running free, his mane and tail flowing in the wind, as he embodied the spirit of the wild and untamed. His bond with the tarweed and the land was deep, and he remained a symbol of freedom and resilience.",
